title: Epilogue
new-page: true
set-bg: img/bg_galaxy.jpg
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.ending) { Q.ending = SW.routeEnding(Q); Q.ending_title = SW.ENDING_TITLES[Q.ending]; }
// Padmé's fate follows Anakin's
if (Q.anakin_fallen && Q.ending !== 'reborn') Q.padme_alive = 0;
// sub-endings
Q.sub_reborn = 'ruusan';
if (Q.rim_enfranchised && (Q.slavery_abolished || Q.rim_relief >= 2)) Q.sub_reborn = 'rim';
else if ((Q.jedi_reformed || Q.jedi_independence) && Q.anakin_found && !Q.anakin_fallen) Q.sub_reborn = 'order';
Q.seeds = (Q.delegation_formed || Q.petition >= 1 || Q.pact_formed) ? 1 : 0;
Q.blood_liberty = (Q.faith >= 50 && Q.emergency_powers <= 4) ? 1 : 0;
this.achieve('ending_' + Q.ending);
if (Q.anakin_found && !Q.anakin_fallen && Q.anakin_fall < 8) this.achieve('anakin_saved');
Q.legacy_html = (typeof SW.legacyHTML === 'function') ? SW.legacyHTML(Q) : '';
Q.summary_html = (typeof SW.summaryHTML === 'function') ? SW.summaryHTML(Q) : '';
Q.game_ach_html = (typeof SW.achievementsHTML === 'function') ? SW.achievementsHTML(Q, true) : '';
Q.game_over_reached = 1;
!}
go-to: ep_reborn if ending = "reborn"; ep_endures if ending = "endures"; ep_blood if ending = "blood"; ep_divided if ending = "divided"; ep_protectorate if ending = "protectorate"; ep_admirals if ending = "admirals"; ep_hollow if ending = "hollow_crown"; ep_confederacy if ending = "confederacy"; ep_dissolved if ending = "dissolved"; ep_endless if ending = "endless_war"; ep_empire if ending = "empire"

@ep_reborn
go-to: legacy

= The Republic Reborn

The trial of Darth Sidious lasts a year. The galaxy watches every day of it. When it ends, the Senate does something it has not done in a generation: it reforms itself. The emergency powers are gone and the Chancellery shrinks to its old size. Committee by committee, the Senate takes back the authority it gave away.

[? if sub_reborn = "ruusan" : **A New Ruusan.** A constitutional convention meets on Coruscant, a thousand years after the last one. Its charter binds every future Chancellor: term limits no emergency can break, powers that expire unless renewed, an army that answers to the Senate. Schoolchildren on a million worlds will learn its preamble by heart: *"Never again shall the Republic vote away its freedom."* ?][? if sub_reborn = "rim" : **The Rim Enfranchised.** For the first time in its history, the Republic belongs to the Outer Rim as much as to the Core. Rim senators chair committees. The slave markets are gone. Worlds that once cheered Dooku's speeches send delegations to Coruscant, and many seceded systems vote, one by one, to come home. ?][? if sub_reborn = "order" : **The Order Renewed.** The Jedi Order, shaken to its foundations, chooses to change. It becomes once more a guardian of peace, not an army. It accepts that its Knights may love, as long as they do not hide it. Anakin Skywalker, Jedi Master, is among those who rewrite its Code. ?]

It is not a perfect Republic. It is still slow, quarrelsome and sometimes corrupt. But it is free, and it knows now how close it came to losing that.

@ep_endures
go-to: legacy

= The Republic Endures

[? if shadow_remains : Chancellor Palpatine leaves office at the end of his term, his powers stripped and his name tarnished by everything the Caucus put on the record. He is never charged. He retires to Naboo, and the Jedi never learn what he was. Somewhere, a shadow remains, and it is patient. ?][? if not shadow_remains : The Sith Lord is gone, but much of what he built remains. ?] [? if emergency_powers >= 3 : The Chancellery keeps many of the powers he took, though it uses them more gently now. ?][? if corruption >= 60 : The Senate is as corrupt as ever, and the guilds as greedy. ?][? if faith < 50 : Faith in the Republic is shaken, perhaps for good. ?]

Still, the Republic endures. Its Senate still meets. Its senators still argue. And somewhere in the Caucus offices on Coruscant, a new generation of reformers is already planning the next fight, knowing now how close the last one came.

@ep_blood
go-to: legacy

= Victory in Blood

The War for the Republic ends with Darth Sidious in chains and the Free Republic's banners over Coruscant. It cost millions of lives, the Jedi Order, and a generation's innocence.

[? if blood_liberty : **Liberty Restored.** The victors keep their promises. The emergency powers are repealed, the Senate restored, and the generals sent home. The Republic that rises from the ashes is poorer and scarred, but it is a republic. ?][? if not blood_liberty : **The Admirals' Shadow.** The generals who won the war are in no hurry to give it back. The Republic survives in name, guarded by the very men and women who saved it, and it is not yet clear whether they will ever leave. ?]

@ep_divided
go-to: legacy

= The Galaxy Divided

[? if empire_declared or sidious_free : The Galactic Empire rules the Core from Coruscant. ?][? if not empire_declared and not sidious_free : The Sith Lord's regime holds Coruscant and the Core. ?] Against it stands the **Free Republic**: Alderaan, Chandrila, Corellia, Mon Cala and much of the Rim, governed by the senators who walked out of the rotunda rather than applaud.

The war will last for years, perhaps decades. But the Republic was not voted out of existence. It lives on wherever people still choose to govern themselves, and as long as it lives, the Empire has not won.

@ep_protectorate
go-to: legacy

= The Jedi Protectorate

The Sith are gone, destroyed by the Jedi. So, in all but name, is the Senate. The Jedi Council governs "temporarily" through a Senate that meets only to ratify its decisions. Its Knights are wise, mostly. They are also unelected and answerable to no one but themselves.

Mace Windu promises that power will be returned "when the danger has passed". The Caucus has heard those words before. In a cantina on Corellia, an old senator named Bel Iblis is already drafting the first manifesto of a new resistance.

@ep_admirals
go-to: legacy

= The Admirals' Republic

[? if admirals_coup : Wilhuff Tarkin's Council of Admirals rules "until victory", and victory never quite comes. The Senate is suspended, then recalled as an advisory chamber. Somewhere in the Chancellery district, a retired senator from Naboo offers the admirals his counsel, and they are wise enough to take it. ?][? if not admirals_coup : Darth Sidious is gone, but the machine he built runs on without him. The emergency powers, the regional governors and the security services pass to the men who served him: Vice Chair Mas Amedda, Governor Tarkin, the admirals of the Grand Army. They speak of order, stability and the dangers of the Jedi. ?]

The Republic survives in name. The Senate still meets, when it is allowed to. It is not the Empire. But it is not the Republic the Caucus fought for, either.

@ep_hollow
go-to: legacy

= The Hollow Crown

Our Chancellor keeps the emergency powers "for now", to rebuild, to keep order, to make sure the Sith never return. The Caucus tells itself that this is different, because we are the good ones.

A year passes, then five. The powers are never returned. The Caucus's own reformers become the Chancellery's loyalists, and the next generation of reformers learns to fear us. In the end the Sith did not need to win. We did it for them.

@ep_confederacy
go-to: legacy

= Confederacy Triumphant

[? if cis_negotiated : The war never ends on a battlefield. The front collapses one system at a time, until the Senate, exhausted and afraid, votes to negotiate. ?] The Republic sues for peace. The Treaty of Raxus hands the Rim, the Mid Rim and the trade lanes to the Confederacy of Independent Systems, and leaves a shrunken, humiliated Republic clinging to the Core.

The Confederacy is not the free federation Dooku promised. It is ruled by the guilds, the Banking Clan and the Techno Union, and its parliament is a facade. Behind them all, a hooded figure is satisfied. He has a galaxy at war with itself, and both halves in his debt.

@ep_dissolved
go-to: legacy

= A Republic Dissolved

[? if recognized_cis : The Treaty of Separation ends the Clone Wars. ?][? if not recognized_cis : The Republic does not go to war. It simply comes apart. ?] The Separatist worlds go their own way, and the Republic that remains is smaller, poorer and humbled. It has lost half the galaxy and a thousand years of pride.

But it is still a republic. Its Senate still meets, and its Chancellor still answers to it. Without his war, the Sith Lord's grand design has no foundation. Perhaps, one day, the worlds that left will want to come home to something better.

@ep_endless
go-to: legacy

= The Endless War

The Clone Wars do not end. Neither side can win, and neither will yield. Year after year the front moves a few systems one way, then back again. The clones age twice as fast as the men who ordered them, and the factories on Kamino never stop.

[? if sidious_defeated : The Sith Lord is gone, but the war he started has outlived him. The guilds that profit from it on both sides have no reason to let it stop. ?][? if not sidious_defeated : In the Chancellery, the man who started it waits. Every year of war makes the Senate more afraid, and every frightened Senate gives him a little more. He has time. ?]

The Republic survives as a war state: rationing on the Rim, recruiting posters on Coruscant, and a Senate that meets mostly to renew the emergency. Children are born who have never known peace. The Caucus fights on, for budgets and for ceasefires that never hold.

@ep_empire
go-to: legacy

= The Galactic Empire

*"So this is how liberty dies,"* Padmé Amidala said. *"With thunderous applause."*

The Republic is gone. In its place stands the Galactic Empire of Emperor Palpatine. [? if order66 : The Jedi have been exterminated, all but a handful of exiles. ?] [? if anakin_fallen : At the Emperor's side stands a figure in black armour, Darth Vader, who was once Anakin Skywalker. ?] [? if not padme_alive : Padmé Amidala is dead. ?] The Senate survives for a while, as a ceremony.

[? if seeds : **Seeds of Rebellion.** But the Caucus has not been destroyed, only scattered. Bail Organa returns to Alderaan, Mon Mothma to Chandrila. In secret, the senators who stood against the New Order begin to talk again: of alliances, of hidden fleets, of a rebellion. The Republic is gone, but not forgotten. ?][? if not seeds : Of the Caucus, little remains: a few senators who keep their heads down, and a few who are never heard from again. ?]

@legacy
game-over: true

